            <ArticleTitle>Effect of N- and C-terminal functional groups on the stability of collagen triple helices.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11036-11039</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc05837c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect of charged versus neutral N- and C-termini on the stability of the collagen triple helix was examined. Thermal denaturation studies at different pH with collagen model peptides showed that an ammonium group at the N-terminus destabilizes the triple helix more than a carboxylate at the C-terminus. A neutral carboxylic acid stabilizes the triple helix more than an amido moiety at the C-terminus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
